<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Option flowmode (GH-780): ARM code that control flow proves the mode of is
    painted with that mode where the Listing walk's own blx writes left the
    other one.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture. The script loads
    the stripped fixture `arm_interwork_le32` (generator beside it) twice with
    the Listing walk on, as every CLI surface runs it on ARM: an A32 entry at
    0x2000000 runs `blx 0x2000040` (a Thumb `movs r0,#7; bx lr`) and then
    `bl 0x2000080` (an A32 `add r0,r0,#1; bx lr`). No symbol or mapping
    symbol names either mode.

    Pass 1, option off: decoding the `blx` wrote Thumb into the context
    database from 0x2000040 to the end of the address space, so the A32
    helper decodes as Thumb and the decompiler prints `halt_missing()` for it
    (a Thumb decode starting at 0x2000082).

    Pass 2, the default: the entry's even address proves A32, the `blx`
    proves Thumb for its own target, the Thumb helper returns, so the `bl`
    after it is proven too and its target keeps A32. That target is painted
    A32: the A32 helper returns `a0 + 1` and the entry passes the Thumb
    result to it.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/arm_interwork_le32</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option flowmode off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000080</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/arm_interwork_le32</com>
  <com>option listing on</com>
  <com>option flowmode on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000080</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000040</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2000000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #1: off, the blx write makes the A32 helper decode as Thumb" min="1" max="1">halt_missing</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #2: on, the bl target keeps the A32 mode and returns a0 + 1" min="1" max="1">return a0 \+ 1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #3: on, the blx target decodes as Thumb and returns 7" min="1" max="1">return 7;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="FLOWMODE #4: on, the entry passes the Thumb result to the A32 helper" min="1" max="1">sub_2000080\(sub_2000040\(\)\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
